Z||000000||Omnipotence||11-29-2000||07:03 PM||||thinking of puting dvd in my fiero and need some ideas. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Loki||11-29-2000||07:51 PM||||It all depends on what  your looking to get out of the multi-media setup..There are several companies that make DVD systems...Some make an all in one unit (screen player and chassis) others are all seperate units, which means finding more mounting spots and more wires.....Other than choosing what you want its a straight forward install, just like a radio. I did have an Alpine in-dash 5.8" lcd screen in my Fiero and I liked it but in the limited space of the Fiero it got old fast.......Also other things to consider are the laws...In most states (USA) its illegal to have a screen in view of the driver......<P>Loki<P>Loki137@home.Com||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||11-29-2000||08:29 PM||||not a good idea to have a dvd in any vehicle in my opinion.  except maybe in a van in the back.  but in a fiero, i wouldn't even consider it.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-29-2000||11:03 PM||||I had a system design all worked out for a DVD/GPS/TV system in a Fiero. I would put a flat screen monitor in the dash map pocket, and glass it in. I would then put the Alpine DVD player under the dash, in front of the passenger seat. Or, you could get a setup with the screen comming out of the headunit and folding up, but I dont like that as well. Email me, I think we could help you out alot on a design like this. I would love to see it in play. It could be done easily enough, if your willing to part with the money it takes for these type of thigs. sean@kdsi.net is my address.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||11-30-2000||09:18 AM||||Why not mount the DVD player where your radio is?<P> <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-jFIgK332JMf/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=39600&I=133DVR909&o=&a=" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-jFIgK332JMf/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=39600&I=133DVR909&o=&a=</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||11-30-2000||05:53 PM||||Same type thing I had in my head, But, a system of seperate units would cost less then that, and give you more features. With that unit you would still have to mount a screen somewhere in the car. That is a nice unit, but wow, $1699 for it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||12-01-2000||09:35 PM||||I work at CompUSA, and we have an audiovox portable dvd player for 549, even has dolby digital out, and a composite video out.. just a thought. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
